<!-- orchestration:start -->
## Enforced Orchestration Contract

This session's orchestration workflow is mechanically enforced by
`~/.claude/hooks/orchestration/orchestrator-gate.cjs` (installed by the
`claude-codex-orca-orchestration` installer), not merely described here. Full contract,
config reference and escape hatches: `~/.claude/rules/orchestration-contract.md`.

Summary — every value is config-driven (`~/.claude/orchestration.config.json`), so treat
the SessionStart banner printed each session as the exact current numbers, not this file:

- The main panel orchestrates only: it dispatches and supervises, and does not itself
  Edit/Write or run mutating shell commands outside `.claude/`, `plans/`, `docs/`, scratch.
- Planning, review and verification run on the configured review model, in-session.
- **Coder pool:** Code goes to Codex in an Orca worker first, then the configured
  in-session code model once Codex is unusable or has used its configured handoff
  percentage of quota (default 95). This covers code, builds, refactors, tests, bulk
  conversions, and fix loops. The operator can override with
  `--code-model <alias|codex|codex:<model>|auto>` or the `--exec-*` shortcuts.
- Codex listed in `disabledCoders` (or `ORCH_DISABLED_CODERS`) receives no new work: it is
  not availability-probed or routed, its `--code-model`/`--exec-*` override is ignored, and
  its `worker-start` is refused. Existing live workers remain heartbeat quota-checked; parked
  workers do not auto-resume until the coder is enabled again.
- Every code brief names a verify command.
- A heartbeat daemon must supervise any live Orca worker; `Stop` refuses to end the
  session with one still live and unwatched.

Escape hatches (operator-only): `ORCHESTRATOR_GATE=off` (env), `--no-orchestrate` (prompt).
<!-- orchestration:end -->
